# Google style, at 100 columns.
#
# 100 rather than Google's 80 because that is what the codebase already is: the
# p99 line is 99 characters and 1660 lines exceed 80. Reflowing to 80 would have
# rewritten far more than adopting the tool needs to.
#
# Everything else is stock Google on purpose. Measured over all 85 tracked C++
# files, every attempt to preserve the old hand-aligned columns made the diff
# BIGGER, not smaller (6199 lines -> 8251 with AlignConsecutive*), because
# clang-format aligns every consecutive run rather than the specific places a
# human chose to. There is no config that keeps the hand style, so this file
# does not pretend otherwise. See #47.
BasedOnStyle: Google
ColumnLimit: 100
